id":28077,"sitename":"Lehmilampi","sitedescription":"Small lake. Physiography: depression. Surrounding vegetation: pine and spruce.","sitenotes":"sampling date 2004 to 2007, diameter of coring 5 to 6.5cm, Data source Mazier, F. for Landclim Project","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[29.1,63.61667]}","altitude":116,"collectionunitid":37931,"collectionunit":"Lehmilampi core","handle":"LEM","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/xhe0-eq85","10.21233/XHE0-EQ85"],"agerange":[{"units":"Varve years BP","ageold":5344,"ageyoung":28}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":52093,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"F.","contactid":11484,"firstname":"Florence","familyname":"Mazier","contactname":"Mazier, Florence"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Data submitted by Mazier, F.tor Landclim Project and submitted by gaillard, M.J. to the EPD.","recdatecreated":"2021-10-21T14:42:05"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":30965,"sitename":"Palomaa","sitedescription":"Small mire located close to the northern limit of pine forest in eastern Finnish Lapland. To the south, forest areas are dominated almost exclusively by Scots Pine (Pinus sylvestris) while, to the north, the regional vegetation type is mountain birch woodland (Betula pubescens ssp. czerepanovii).","sitenotes":"String fen in which the strings are not well developed but rather occur as Sphagnum fuscum hummocks with Betula nana, Empetrum nigrum, Vaccinium uliginosum, V. oxycoccus, Ledum palustre, Andromeda polifolia and Rubus chamaemorus, separated by flark areas dominated by Eriophorum vaginatum, Trichophorum caespitosum and Carex spp. There is one extensive pool, some smaller areas of standing water and a stream that drains the mire towards the east.","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[27.19048,69.2778]}","altitude":200,"collectionunitid":42184,"collectionunit":"Palomaa core","handle":"PALOMAA","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":[],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":58529,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"T.","contactid":9628,"firstname":"Tomasz","familyname":"Goslar","contactname":"Goslar, Tomasz"}],"datasettype":"geochronologic","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2024-04-11T13:38:58"},{"doi":["10.21233/d49m-jd45","10.21233/MKRP-9818"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":878.26,"ageyoung":-54.58}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":58530,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":18392,"firstname":"Andreas","familyname":"Lücke","contactname":"Lücke, Andreas"},{"initials":"F.","contactid":4065,"firstname":"Friederike","familyname":"Wagner-Cremer","contactname":"Wagner-Cremer, Friederike"},{"initials":"H.","contactid":17070,"firstname":"Heidi","familyname":"Hyyppä","contactname":"Hyyppä, Heidi"},{"initials":"K.","contactid":19530,"firstname":"Kristian","familyname":"Schoning","contactname":"Schoning, Kristian"},{"initials":"S.P.","contactid":1091,"firstname":"Sheila P.","familyname":"Hicks","contactname":"Hicks, Sheila P."},{"initials":"T.","contactid":9628,"firstname":"Tomasz","familyname":"Goslar","contactname":"Goslar, Tomasz"},{"initials":"W.","contactid":8772,"firstname":"Walter","familyname":"Finsinger","contactname":"Finsinger, Walter"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"The samples are consecutive and aim at representing around 1 year. Thus, pollen percentages should be usied with caution. We recommend to amalgamate samples together and calculate averages prior to calculating pollen percentages.","recdatecreated":"2024-04-11T13:39:03"},{"doi":["10.21233/2256-QP08"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":878.26,"ageyoung":-54.58}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":58533,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":18392,"firstname":"Andreas","familyname":"Lücke","contactname":"Lücke, Andreas"},{"initials":"F.","contactid":4065,"fir