utionary ecology of reproductive modes in non-marine Ostracoda” (1994-1996), primarily to enable mapping of sexual and parthenogenetic reproductive modes.  Further development of NODE has included continued data entry, application of taxonomic revisions, and validation exercises using Google Earth and other online resources to check, correct and refine the coordinates of every record. Each record is assigned a Validation Status colour: green (accurate), amber (as good as possible given limitations of published information) or red (uncertain or unreliable and in need of further checking). Users are advised to check the Validation Status (in Site Notes) of the data they map and consider eliminating any that are “red”. Species occurrence records are derived mainly from published literature spanning the 19th, 20th and 21st centuries and represent specimens that were (or are assumed to have been) collected alive. Taxonomic names have been updated in accordance with the global checklist of Meisch et al. (2024: https://doi.org/10.5852/ejt.2024.974.2767) but NODE also includes the original “Name in Reference” as given in the source of the occurrence record (see Collection Unit Notes).\\nNODE records include additional metadata such as environmental classifications of sites and taxonomic/nomenclatural comments that are being prepared for future import to Neotoma.","recdatecreated":"2026-02-13T23:52:44"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":37988,"sitename":"South Of Ekenas + Loc. 14","sitedescription":null,"sitenotes":"Validation status: amber(see Dataset Notes)","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[23.43833,59.96222]}","altitude":null,"collectionunitid":51456,"collectionunit":"NODE-R3504","handle":"NODE-R3504","unittype":"Modern","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/xmjq-jj32"],"agerange":[],"database":"Nonmarine Ostracod Distribution in Europe Database","datasetid":69998,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"L.","contactid":218